   "title": "10 Nigerian Startups To Showcase Homegrown Innovations In Singapore",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/10-nigerian-startups-to-showcase-homegrown-innovations-in-singapore/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:56:35 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792983395.0,
   "ageDays": 0.05,
   "summary": "Ten Nigerian startups are set to showcase their innovations at the APAC Summit 2026 in Singapore on 30th October, seeking partnerships and opportunities to expand into the Asia-Pacific market. Selected under the NIMENA programme, the startups will present solutions spanning financial technology, agriculture, healthcare, logistics, education, security and digital media to international businesses, investors and innovation partners. The APAC Summit 2026 will take place in Singapore on 30 October.",
   "summary_zh": "10家尼日利亚初创企业将于10月30日在新加坡举行的2026年亚太峰会上展示其创新成果，寻求合作伙伴关系和拓展亚太市场的机会。这些初创企业是在NIMENA计划下入选的，将向国际企业、投资者和创新合作伙伴展示金融科技、农业、医疗保健、物流、教育、安全和数字媒体等领域的解决方案。2026年亚太峰会将于10月30日在新加坡举行。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Ten Nigerian startups are set to showcase their innovations at the APAC Summit 2026 in Singapore on 30th October, seeking partnerships and opportunities to expand into the Asia-Pacific market. Selected under the NIMENA programme, the startups will present solutions spanning financial technology, agriculture, healthcare, logistics, education, security and digital media to international businesses, investors and innovation partners. The initiative, announced by Plug and Play APAC, aims to connect the founders with the wider Asia-Pacific innovation ecosystem and explore opportunities for cross-border collaboration. Their solutions address practical challenges across different sectors. Dojah and Youverify provide identity verification and compliance technology, while Crop2Cash helps smallholder farmers build financial identities to access credit. TradeBuza connects African agricultural producers to international markets. In logistics and security, i-Purvey develops technology to anticipate disruptions in aviation and maritime operations; Shipbubble simplifies deliveries for online merchants; and Sorair deploys automated drone and camera systems to monitor industrial facilities. HealthStack focuses on digital health systems; BeGenio Tech uses game-based learning to improve children’s mathematics skills; and Happaning develops technology that lets viewers choose camera angles during live events. Their participation offers an opportunity to test the commercial potential of these solutions beyond Africa. However, success will depend on their ability to secure local partners, meet regulatory requirements and demonstrate that their products can compete in the Southeast Asian market. The summit is expected to provide a platform for the founders to engage with prospective investors, businesses, and technology partners as they explore potential routes into the region. The APAC Summit 2026 will take place in Singapore on 30 October. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
