   "title": "YPP Presidential Candidate, Agada, Faults FG’s 90-Day Action Plan to Ease Cost of Living",
   "url": "https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/10/25/ypp-presidential-candidate-agada-faults-fgs-90-day-action-plan-to-ease-cost-of-living/",
   "domain": "thisdaylive.com",
   "source": "ThisDay（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:22:15 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792894935.0,
   "ageDays": 1.08,
   "summary": "The presidential candidate of Young Progressives Party (YPP), Mr Peter Agada, has faulted the federal government’s 90-day action plan to ease cost of living, describing it as a campaign strategy that did not reflect economic reality. The Minister of Finance and Coordinating Minister of Economy, Mr. Taiwo Oyedele, had announced that the National Executive Council (NEC) approved a 90-day plan to cushion the high cost of living on Nigerians.",
   "summary_zh": "青年进步党（YPP）总统候选人彼得·阿加达先生批评联邦政府旨在缓解生活成本的90天行动计划，称该计划是一项没有反映经济现实的竞选策略。财政部长兼经济协调部长泰沃·奥耶德莱先生此前宣布，全国执行委员会（NEC）批准了一项90天计划，以缓解尼日利亚人面临的高生活成本。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The presidential candidate of Young Progressives Party (YPP), Mr Peter Agada, has faulted the federal government’s 90-day action plan to ease cost of living, describing it as a campaign strategy that did not reflect economic reality. Agada said the President Bola Tinubu’s administration had failed after introducing numerous economic measures without results. The Minister of Finance and Coordinating Minister of Economy, Mr. Taiwo Oyedele, had announced that the National Executive Council (NEC) approved a 90-day plan to cushion the high cost of living on Nigerians. Reacting in an interview in Abuja, Agada said the economic team of the President had lost focus. “I align with those who opine that the economic team of Mr. President has failed to address Nigeria’s numerous economic challenges. I have listened to many analysts, but none spoke positively in support of the economic team,” he said. He noted that the minister had earlier announced subsidy intervention and a 17-point plan, including reduction of pump price, removal of illegal levies, but nothing was done, prompting resort to a 90-day timeline. “These promises back and forth are for Nigerians to believe and vote them back into office. If you believe in the rules of the game they are playing, there are just 85 days to election, and you are saying a 90-day timeline to cushion the cost of living. So, after the election, what happens? These guys are playing mind games,” he said. He said the government later removed tariffs on food importation which did not fight food inflation but only affected calculation. “If you said you were fighting food inflation, then return food prices to where they were before you took office,” he said. He further alleged that import waiver cuts pushed customs revenue to N35 trillion with about 60 per cent for military hardware importation without accounting. As an alternative, Agada recommended his Labour-Direct ward-to-ward development strategy, which he said can empower Nigerians with N40 million monthly and capture all Nigerians within 60 days of implementation. “Labour-Direct, ward-to-ward strategy remains an option that can capture all Nigerians within 60 days. At the moment, they have to take a look at our ward-to-ward plan. If they approach me to implement a 60-day development plan, Nigerians will have more confidence,” he said. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
