   "url": "https://x.com/igeostrategic/status/2113726224052707608",
   "snippet": "🔘 US Security Analysis Warns of ISIS-Sahel Networks Extending Toward Morocco and Spain\n\nRabat | October 23, 2026\n\nA security analysis published by the US-based platform Lawfare on October 18 highlights the evolving transnational threat posed by Islamic State networks operating across Africa's Sahel region, including potential links to Morocco and Spain.\n\nThe assessment examines recruitment, financing and remote operational coordination, drawing on counterterrorism investigations and previously disrupted networks.\n\nThe warning comes amid persistent jihadist violence in the Sahel. Reuters reported that at least 48 civilians were killed in attacks in eastern Mali attributed by local sources to Islamic State-linked militants.\n\nFor Morocco, these developments underscore the strategic importance of preventive intelligence, cross-border security cooperation and early disruption of extremist networks.\n\nThe available reporting does not establish an imminent terrorist attack in Morocco.\n\n#Morocco #SahelSecurity #Counterterrorism #StrategicInsight #NajibStrategy #NajibCommunication",
